  "published": "2026-10-18T13:11:53.047Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.4.0: a platform authorization view, and what the WebAuthn Signal API needs from the server. New Razor component MyIdentityAuthorizePlatformView (MyIdentity.Components), the platform counterpart of MyIdentityAuthorizeView: it renders ChildContent or NotAuthorized from IMyIdentityPlatformPermissionService.HasPlatformPermissionAsync and asks again only when ModuleCode or PermissionRequired changes, not when its parent re-renders; PermissionRequired None throws. An AuthorizeView with MyIdentityPolicies.PlatformPermission or MyIdentityPolicies.Permission authorizes again, usually with a query, on every parameter pass, and while it waits takes what it authorized out of the tree, so that content comes back as new instances: for a fragment whose parent re-renders, use the new component, or MyIdentityAuthorizeView for a tenant permission. For the WebAuthn Signal API: MyIdentityLoginResult.PasskeyCredentialUnknown is true only for a passkey sign-in refused because no row of the passkey table holds the signed credential (Status stays InvalidCredentials; the answer does not depend on the user handle), and the static MyIdentityPasskeyUserEntity gives the user handle (UserHandle) and the name (Name) the library registers passkeys with. Behaviour change: when Identity refuses the assertion and the store does not hold the credential, the sign-in audit log records PasskeyNotFound, without an account, instead of AssertionFailed. The package validation baseline is 5.3.0. Upgrading from 5.3.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §48.",
